  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Request**\n\nOkay, I\'m carefully dissecting the user\'s request. The goal is to act as a software engineer and update the logic of a financial calculator. This calculator helps clients see the potential savings by adopting a predictive device to mitigate logistics losses. I\'m focusing on the specifics of the calculator\'s function and the client\'s perspective.\n\n\n**Defining Input Parameters**\n\nI\'ve defined the necessary input fields for the calculator: total cargo weight (kg), average value per kilogram (R$/kg), and a selector for the goods\' state (\"Frozen\" or \"Refrigerated\"). Now, I\'m integrating the specific business rules for estimating financial waste in the backend. I\'m focusing on the calculations: Total Cargo Value (weight x value/kg), and the fixed 12% loss due to temperature failures.\n\n\n**Calculating Evaporation Loss**\n\nI\'m now integrating the humidity-based loss calculation. For \"Refrigerated\" goods, a 2% weight loss, due to dehydration, will be subtracted from the total weight. This weight loss is then multiplied by the value per kilogram to get the financial impact. I am thinking of adding this figure with the thermal breakdown in an output \"Estimated Waste Avoided\". I will also show the details of the cold chain and moisture-related savings.\n\n\n"
