  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the prompt\'s scope**\n\nI\'m digging into the user\'s prompt, focusing on the software engineering aspect and the need to update the loss mitigation financial calculator\'s logic. I\'m aiming to grasp the scope of the updates needed for this financial tool. I\'m determining which are the key functionalities that are expected to be updated, and preparing to define the objectives of the logic update.\n\n\n**Defining input parameters**\n\nI\'ve defined the input fields for the calculator: total cargo weight (kg), average value per kg (R$/kg), and a state selector (\"Frozen\" or \"Refrigerated\"). Now, I\'m working to calculate the estimated financial waste. The goal is to provide these calculations clearly for the customer.\n\n\n**Calculating the Financial Impact**\n\nI\'m now integrating the dehydration losses, setting a safe average range of 1% to 3%, encompassing initial chilling and prolonged storage, into the calculation. This will give the exact money loss. The HTML prototype is helping visualize the UI changes. For the \"Refrigerated\" option, I\'ll highlight the impact of water loss. Finally, I\'ll sum losses due to cold chain breaks and dehydration, displaying the final result as \"Estimated Waste Avoided\".\n\n\n**Refining UI calculations**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on UI representation. I will present calculation updates for the financial impact. The updated calculation will integrate dehydration losses, adding a safe average of 1% to 3% encompassing initial chilling and prolonged storage. I\'m focusing on \"Refrigerated\" cargo, emphasizing the potential for water loss, and calculating the exact money loss. I\'ll sum this to estimate the final \'Waste Avoided\' total.\n\n\n**Formalizing the Calculations**\n\nI\'m now formalizing the calculations precisely. I\'ve defined \"congelada\" and \"resfriada\" states. I\'ve broken down the calculation into steps: calculating gross value, factoring in cold chain break loss (12%), and dehydration loss (2%). If \"resfriada\" is selected, I\'ll flag dehydration as crucial, explaining the significant impact of hydric loss. The total waste avoided is the sum of both loss types (14% total). I am ready to return the payload with calculated values.\n\n\n**Implementing Backend Calculation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the backend calculation via `/api/calculate` using Express. The frontend will fetch from this API, with a local instant fallback to ensure responsiveness. I\'m structuring the calculation result in the UI to display \"Valor Estimado de Desperd\303\255cio Evitado\" with a breakdown of savings from thermal and moisture loss, as well as highlighting the impact of moisture loss in \"Resfriada\" scenarios.\n\n\n**Configuring the Server**\n\nI\'m now adapting the server setup based on the instructions. I will ensure the dev, build, and start scripts in `package.json` are correctly configured. This includes integrating the provided scripts for `tsx server.ts`, the Vite build process with `esbuild`, and the final `node` execution for production. I need to be sure the backend is fully functional.\n\n\n**Updating Server Configuration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided server setup code, implementing the middleware mode for development and static file serving for production. I\'m ensuring correct handling of routes and static assets, and I\'ll now modify the `metadata.json` file. I will rename the app to \"Calculadora de Mitiga\303\247\303\243o de Perdas ColdTrack,\" providing a descriptive description to the user.\n\n\n**Refining UI & Title**\n\nI\'m now synchronizing the `<title>` and `<meta>` tags in `index.html`. Also, I am focusing on the user\'s design and UI elements. I see the prototype styling from \"ColdTrack IoT - Monitoramento da Cadeia do Frio.\" I recognize the simulator (Calculadora de Mitiga\303\247\303\243o de Perdas Log\303\255sticas) and the telemetria dashboard are already in the design. I\'m ensuring the calculator is beautifully crafted and front and center, focusing on the four steps requested.\n\n\n**Calculating Dehydration Impact**\n\nI\'m now implementing the dehydration calculation, focusing on a safe 2% average loss due to evaporation. This calculation complements the thermal loss assessment. I\'m building on the existing backend structure and ensuring the UI will accurately display both loss types. The goal is a clear \"Valor Estimado de Desperd\303\255cio Evitado\" with detailed breakdowns for users to understand.\n\n\n**Finalizing Display and Values**\n\nI\'m now finalizing the display, summing thermal and dehydration losses to calculate \"Valor Estimado de Desperd\303\255cio Evitado.\" I\'m calculating evaporation loss at a 2% rate and highlighting the impact for \"Resfriada\" cargo, emphasizing the high water loss. I\'m providing a breakdown to the user on savings from thermal and moisture loss. I\'ll flag \"Aten\303\247\303\243o Cr\303\255tica\" for \"Resfriada.\"\n\n\n**Adding ROI Metrics**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial ROI metrics based on the predictive IoT device. These include the device\'s cost, the immediate net savings from the trip, the ROI multiplier, and projections for fleet operations and monthly trips. I\'m also planning for PDF report export or an executive summary, providing the full ROI picture.\n\nI\'m checking the styling, and will integrate the appropriate tools and features in the front end.\n\n\n**Integrating Visual Representations**\n\nI\'m now focusing on interactive visualizations. I\'m considering SVG charts using Tailwind and Motion, as they\'re lightweight and responsive, which would require minimal dependencies. I\'m also reviewing the `package.json` scripts and `server.ts` to ensure everything is set up for the backend API. The endpoint will handle the calculation and return the results for the frontend to display. I\'ll focus on the data visualization, as well.\n\n\n**Refining calculation outputs**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the output format. I\'m focusing on the `CalculadoraOutput` interface, ensuring it includes all necessary details. I\'m integrating the dehydration calculations into the final output. My objective is to clearly present the financial impact with specific values, incorporating all variables to ensure an easily digestible format for the expert user.\n```\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 270261361
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
