  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Logo\'s Elements**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently scrutinizing the logo the user uploaded. The shield immediately catches my eye with its dark blue gradient outline. Within the shield, I\'m noting the ice crystal on the left, the thermometer in the center (it\'s a detailed one!), and what appears to be a premium element on the right. I\'m building a mental picture to compare later to user\'s uploaded documents.\n\n\n**Constructing the SafeMeat Logo**\n\nI\'m now focused on building the `SafeMeatLogo` component. I\'m aiming for high-precision SVG to capture every detail, from the cut of meat to the orbital blue swoosh. My plan is to produce both a full badge version and a horizontal header version. The color palette of Navy Blue and Crimson, including exact hex codes, is being integrated to capture a polished result.\n\n\n**Developing the Interface Elements**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing the splash screen and header components. For the splash, I\'m concentrating on a dynamic 1.5-second animation that blends a dark background with a neon-accented logo, title, and slogan. The header will be minimalist and use glass-like backgrounds. I\'m focusing on smooth anchor links to key sections and a prominent \"Fale com um Especialista\" button.\n\n\n**Crafting the Hero Section**\n\nI\'m now deep into the `HeroSection.tsx` component. I\'m focusing on a dark, elegant gradient background with subtle industrial logistics imagery to establish a cold, professional feel. I\'m excited about the headline: \"A Integridade da Cadeia do Frio na Palma da M\303\243o\" and the accompanying subtitle. I\'m carefully constructing the CTA buttons, ensuring smooth scrolling and an elegant modal for the pitch deck. The trust proof bar with cold logistics metrics is coming along well too.\n\n\n**Defining Value Propositions**\n\nI\'ve been working on defining the core value propositions. It seems I will focus on \"Continuous monitoring and reliable auditing, protecting the reputation of producer brands\". I\'ve distilled this into 3 support pillars: \"Certified Food Safety\", \"Financial Risk Mitigation\", and \"Reputation Shielding & Compliance.\"\n\n**Constructing the \"O Que Fazemos\" Section**\n\nI am now designing the \"WhatWeDoSection.tsx\" component. I\'m going with a modern layout of three minimalist cards. Each card contains a tech icon and descriptive text. I\'ve drafted copy, focusing on the real-time sensors, the control dashboard, and data storage for audits.\n\n**Summarizing \"Sobre N\303\263s\"**\n\nI am now focused on the \"AboutUsSection.tsx\", which I\'m working to flesh out with text and design. I\'m including the exact text, a slightly gray background and visual elements or tech pillars. This section highlights our team of Systems Analysis and Development students, and our dedication to using technology to solve logistics challenges, bridging academics and real-world needs.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 18
      nanos: 953632151
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
